winch doc: show the reference

Examples:
  # list the topics and the modules
  winch doc
  # show a topic
  winch doc project
  # show one key of a topic
  winch doc step.when
  # show the keys of a module and an example step
  winch doc file
  # show the full text of one key
  winch doc file.mode
  # show a key of a list element
  winch doc firewall.allow.tcp
  # print the whole reference as JSON
  winch doc --json

Usage:
  winch doc [<topic> | <module>][.<key>...]
  winch doc --json

Doc shows the reference: the index of topics and modules, a topic, the
keys of one module with an example step, or the full text of one key
or function.

It needs no project. The text comes from the definitions that the load
checks use, so it matches the installed version.

An unknown module or key is an error with "did you mean".

Flags:
  --json                      whole reference as one JSON document
